+
+A concrete generated lesson is underidentified. With seed `0`, difficulty `None`, sample indices `4,5,6,7` as four demonstrations and index `8` as the query, this plausible rival fits every demonstration:
+
+> For a pierced color-2 segment, place the right wall immediately after the rightmost color-8 pipe inside the segment.
+
+The selected rule instead places that wall one column after the segment's right edge. All four demonstrations have no case where those positions differ. The query contains segment `7..10` with pipes at columns `7` and `9`; the selected wall is column `11`, while the rival wall is column `10`. Protected Racket executes both complete programs: the rival matches 4/4 demonstrations and changes 18 query cells.
